(text "NUCLEO-32 (STM32G431KB)" (at 281.94 96.52 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 80168526-5172-44dd-9a38-2fd62ca51564))
(text "HAND-WHEEL HALL SENSOR (one magnet: one pulse per stitch)" (at 203.2 198.11999999999998 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 3f4f2626-d047-4102-9166-0c37c51bbafd))
(text "OPERATOR INPUTS (RC-filtered ADC; switches: internal pull-ups)" (at 335.28 27.940000000000005 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 66af6044-a22f-4caa-b7b3-33b84b262e0b))
(text "NOTES (draft, Claude at Bob Drzyzgula's direction, October 2026; not built or tested)" (at 20.32 230.0 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27) bold) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 6fba2062-8492-4957-9177-a1f4aa85e92c))
(text "1. After Freescale AN1662 (Skalka): zero-cross interrupt starts a timer; at the firing angle a short gate pulse (~100 us) fires the triac each half-cycle;" (at 20.32 233.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 9bb1b204-2f28-49b2-a6f2-24fd3b183108))
(text "   tacho period measured by input capture; speed loop updated every half-cycle (120 Hz); stall watchdog. Added here: full isolation, relay, inputs." (at 20.32 237.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid d0696c6b-0b66-4c99-8f39-54f5df8ba727))
(text "2. Pins: ZC on D2/PA12 (EXTI); FIRE on D3/PB0 (TIM3_CH3, one-pulse); HALL on D6/PB6 (TIM4_CH1 input capture); RELAY on D11/PB5;" (at 20.32 240.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 551686af-5bf8-440b-8122-0a30fdbe150b))
(text "   A0-A3 = knee, pedal, FSR, speed limit; NEEDLE on D4/PB7 (SB2 must be OFF); STITCH on D9/PA8. D0/D1 left for the ST-LINK virtual COM port." (at 20.32 244.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 5ab5aada-1ad3-46f8-a474-362dc3a28cc4))
(text "3. Power: PS1 feeds CN3-4 (+5V). Per UM2397 the ST-LINK is then unpowered: program and debug over USB with the mains unplugged." (at 20.32 248.0 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 6ecf4a49-63d1-401e-9d8b-dd66fd5034b1))
(text "   For live debugging use a USB isolator. Never connect a scope ground to the line side." (at 20.32 251.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid a8cbcce6-6a34-43f5-8596-53204832a582))
(text "4. Fire only after a zero-cross has been seen and the speed command is zero (no start on power-up); close K1 last, open it first." (at 20.32 255.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid ace4d766-e479-499a-9966-ab909dee3e50))
(text "5. Values to check: R7/R8 set H11AA1 LED current (~3.9 mA peak at 170 V); R11 gives ~8 mA into U3 from 3.3 V; Q1 needs a heatsink for long runs;" (at 20.32 258.8 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 96afc8b1-3ee5-46e7-b052-105a60e21b02))
(text "   R6/C2 snubber is DNP with a snubberless (BW) triac and fitted if it false-fires; MOV 150 VAC for 120 V mains." (at 20.32 262.4 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 78b2e076-ef84-47d0-839e-4563df02300f))
(text "6. Hall: DRV5023 unipolar switch (open drain) at the hand wheel on a 3-wire cable; one magnet gives one pulse per stitch and needle position." (at 20.32 266.0 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid a1c21a55-6940-42a9-8b22-de825b053ee1))
